<title>FRANCE: Canal Plus shares open up 2.46 percent.</title>
<headline>Canal Plus shares open up 2.46 percent.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Canal Plus opened 2.46 percent higher on the back of an announcement it expected a profit of some three billion francs ($508.5 million) on a television stake swap with Germany's Kirch Group.</p>
<p>The company also said it now expected to make a net profit of close to three billion francs.</p>
<p>At 0809 GMT, Canal Plus was up 1.89 percent at 1,243 while the CAC-40 index of blue-chip shares was down 0.80 percent at 2.913.47. Canal Plus' year-high stands at 1,258 francs.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452 ($ = 5.9 French Francs)</p>
